"""

Structured LLM commentary attached to an AnalysisReport on top of the
deterministic verdict. Strictly additive — the deterministic summary and
recommendation on the parent report remain the authoritative product
surface, and this payload only appears after the analyzer's
verdict-acknowledgement check has passed.
"""
type AiInsights {
    "1–3 sentences describing observations spanning multiple conversion goals. When there is only one goal, the analyzer says so briefly."
    crossGoalPatterns: String!
    "One or two concrete next experiments to consider, grounded in the observed data."
    followUpExperiments: [String!]!
    "1–3 sentences reconciling the observed result against the operator's hypothesis."
    hypothesisAssessment: String!
    "Common bucketing/tracking failure modes to investigate first. Populated only when the deterministic verdict is SRM_FAILED."
    srmRootCauseHints: String
}

"""

An automated analysis report for an experiment.

`summary` and `recommendation` are the deterministic prose written by the
statistical pipeline (chi-squared / Welch's t / Bonferroni) and are the
authoritative product surface for the verdict. `details` is the structured
per-goal/per-variation breakdown the admin UI uses to render tables.

`aiInsights` is an OPTIONAL structured commentary payload written by the
LLM analyzer on top of the deterministic result. It is strictly additive
and labeled as AI in the UI: the analysis job never replaces
summary/recommendation with AI output, and the analyzer rejects any LLM
response whose internal verdict-acknowledgement guardrail does not match
the deterministic verdict, so the AI section can never silently
contradict the deterministic decision. Null when no AI analyzer is wired
or when the verifier rejected the response.
"""
type AnalysisReport {
    aiInsights: AiInsights
    confidence: Float
    created: DateTime!
    details: JSON!
    experimentId: UUID!
    id: UUID!
    recommendation: String!
    summary: String!
}

