ACTIVE at any time (R8) — enforced both at the database layer (a
partial unique index on `board_id where state = 'active'`) and at
the service layer (so the typed `SprintAlreadyActiveException`
surfaces before the SQL would).
"""
enum WorkOpsSprintState {
    ACTIVE
    CLOSED
    FUTURE
}

"""

Phase 3 ships the read shape of WorkOpsWorkflow / WorkOpsWorkflowState /
WorkOpsWorkflowTransition (WorkOpsStatus was added in Phase 2). The JSONB-backed
Conditions / Validators / PostFunctions trees ride opaque through
the GraphQL surface as `JSON` payloads — Phase 7 (admin author UI)
adds a typed builder on top.
"""
enum WorkOpsStatusCategory {
    CANCELLED
    DONE
    IN_PROGRESS
    TODO
}

"""

How a board groups rows. `PROJECT` is the cross-project swimlane
strategy from R30; `QUERY` is Phase 6 (saved-filter swimlanes).
Phase 5 supports `NONE`, `ASSIGNEE`, `EPIC`, `PRIORITY`, `PROJECT`.
"""
enum WorkOpsSwimlaneStrategy {
    ASSIGNEE
    EPIC
    NONE
    PRIORITY
    PROJECT
    QUERY
}

"""

Where in the parent / child hierarchy a task type sits. The numeric
ordering is significant: parents must be at a strictly higher level
than children (R7).
"""
enum WorkOpsTaskHierarchyLevel {
    EPIC
    INITIATIVE
    STANDARD
    SUBTASK
}

"The lifecycle phase of a workflow state"
enum WorkflowStateType {
    "Content is advertised/promoted to users"
    ADVERTISED
    "Content is awaiting approval from a reviewer"
    APPROVAL
    "Content has been approved by a reviewer"
    APPROVED
    "Content is in draft/editing phase"
    DRAFT
    "A workflow processing step has failed"
    FAILURE
    "Content is pending initial processing"
    PENDING
    "Content is being actively processed by a workflow"
    PROCESSING
    "Content is published and visible to end users"
    PUBLISHED
}

enum WorklogVisibility {
    ALL
    PROFILES
    ROLE
}

"A slightly refined version of RFC-3339 compliant DateTime Scalar"
scalar DateTime

"A JSON scalar"
scalar JSON

"A 64-bit signed integer"
scalar Long

"A universally unique identifier compliant UUID Scalar"
scalar UUID

"A file upload scalar"
scalar Upload

"Input for adding a review comment anchored to a diff line."
input AddGitReviewCommentInput {
    commitSha: String!
    content: String!
    filePath: String!
    newLineNumber: Int
    oldLineNumber: Int
    pullRequestId: UUID!
    reviewId: UUID!
}

input AddWorkOpsReleaseGateInput {
    bqlExpression: String
    gateType: String!
    name: String!
    releaseId: UUID!
}

"Input for creating or updating an AI agent definition"
input AgentInput {
    "Optional JSON configuration for additional agent settings such as temperature, max tokens, or custom parameters"
    configuration: JSON
    "Human-readable description of this agent's purpose and capabilities"
    description: String!
    "Unique key used to reference this agent programmatically"
    key: String!
    "The unique identifier of the AI model this agent should use for inference"
    modelId: UUID!
    "Display name for the agent"
    name: String!
    "The unique identifier of the prompt (system instructions) this agent should use"
    promptId: UUID!
}

"Input for creating or updating an agent tool definition"
input AgentToolInput {
    "Optional JSON configuration for additional tool settings, parameters, or connection details"
    configuration: JSON
    "Human-readable description of what this tool does, used to help the AI agent understand when and how to use it"
    description: String!
    "Unique key used to reference this tool programmatically"
    key: String!
    "Optional reference to an MCP server that provides this tool's capabilities"
    mcpServerId: UUID
    "Display name for the tool"
    name: String!
    "Optional reference to a script that implements this tool's behavior"
    scriptId: UUID
}

"Input for creating or updating an analytics dashboard"
input AnalyticsDashboardInput {
    "Optional JSON configuration for dashboard-level layout, theming, or behavior settings"
    configuration: JSON
    "Human-readable description of what this dashboard shows"
    description: String!
    "Existing dashboard ID for updates; omit or null when creating a new dashboard"
    id: UUID
    "Unique string key used to reference this dashboard programmatically"
    key: String!
    "Human-readable display name for this dashboard"
    name: String!
    "User-facing parameter definitions for shared filters"
    parameters: [AnalyticsQueryParameterInput!]
    "Ordered list of visualization instances to display on this dashboard"
    visualizations: [AnalyticsVisualizationInstanceInput!]!
}

"""

Typed device snapshot used by `evaluate` / `evaluateAll`. See the
Kotlin `bosca.analytics.model.Device` class and `Device.attributeValue`
for the canonical field set, alias table, and rules around adding new
keys. Distinct from the `DeviceInput` declared by the `devices`
framework module.
"""
input AnalyticsDevice {
    installationId: String
    manufacturer: String
    model: String
    platform: String
    primaryLocale: String
    systemName: String
    timezone: String
    type: String
    version: String
}

"A named parameter value to pass when executing an analytics query"
input AnalyticsQueryExecutionParameterInput {
    "The parameter identifier matching a parameter defined on the query"
    parameter: String
    "The value to bind to the parameter, as a JSON-compatible value"
    value: JSON
}

"Input for creating or updating an analytics query definition"
input AnalyticsQueryInput {
    "Optional JSON configuration controlling query behavior, formatting, or execution options"
    configuration: JSON
    "Human-readable description of what this query does"
    description: String!
    "Existing query ID for updates; omit or null when creating a new query"
    id: UUID
    "Unique string key used to reference this query programmatically"
    key: String!
    "Human-readable display name for this query"
    name: String!
    "Ordered list of parameter definitions that this query accepts"
    parameters: [AnalyticsQueryParameterInput!]!
    "The raw query string to execute (e.g. SQL or domain-specific query language)"
    query: String!
}

"Input for creating or updating an analytics query parameter definition"
input AnalyticsQueryParameterInput {
    "When type is ARRAY, specifies the data type of elements within the array"
    arrayType: QueryParameterType
    "Default value used when no explicit value is provided at execution time"
    defaultValue: JSON
    "Human-readable description of what this parameter controls"
    description: String!
    "Human-readable display name for this parameter"
    name: String!
    "Unique parameter identifier used as the placeholder name in the query string"
    parameter: String!
    "Whether this parameter must be supplied when executing the query"
    required: Boolean
    "The data type of this parameter's value"
    type: QueryParameterType!
}

"Input for creating or updating an analytics visualization definition"
input AnalyticsVisualizationInput {
    "Optional JSON configuration for chart options, styling, axis labels, color schemes, and other rendering settings"
    configuration: JSON
    "Human-readable description of what this visualization shows"
    description: String!
    "Existing visualization ID for updates; omit or null when creating a new visualization"
    id: UUID
    "Unique string key used to reference this visualization programmatically"
    key: String!
    "Human-readable display name for this visualization"
    name: String!
    "The ID of the analytics query whose results this visualization renders; null for non-data visualizations"
    queryId: UUID
    "The chart or display type used to render this visualization"
    type: AnalyticsVisualizationType!
}

"Input for placing a visualization instance on a dashboard"
input AnalyticsVisualizationInstanceInput {
    "Optional JSON configuration overriding or extending the visualization's default configuration for this placement"
    configuration: JSON
    "The ID of the visualization definition to place on the dashboard"
    visualizationId: UUID!
}

"Input for creating a new API token"
input ApiTokenInput {
    "Group IDs to restrict this token to. Must be a subset of the principal's groups. Omit for all groups."
    allowedGroups: [UUID!]
    "Optional description of this token's intended use"
    description: String
    "When this token should expire. Omit for no expiration."
    expiresAt: DateTime
    "Human-readable name for the token (e.g. 'CI Deploy Token')"
    name: String!
    "Scopes to restrict this token's permissions. Omit for unrestricted access."
    scopes: [String!]
}

"Filter for selecting specific attribute keys from a JSON attributes object, with support for nested filtering"
input AttributesFilterInput {
    "List of top-level attribute keys to include in the result"
    attributes: [String!]!
    "Optional nested filter to apply to child attributes within the selected keys"
    childAttributes: AttributesFilterInput
}

"""

Configurable prior distributions for Bayesian analysis. Null on
the parent experiment means "use sane defaults" (uniform Beta(1,1)
and a flat Normal on event-count means), so operators do not have
to configure anything to get reasonable Bayesian output.
"""
input BayesianPriorInput {
    "Beta prior alpha. Default 1.0 (uniform)."
    betaPriorAlpha: Float
    "Beta prior beta. Default 1.0 (uniform)."
    betaPriorBeta: Float
    "Normal prior mean for EVENT_COUNT goals. Null = improper flat prior."
    normalPriorMean: Float
    "Normal prior variance for EVENT_COUNT goals. Null = improper flat prior."
    normalPriorVariance: Float
}

"Input for initiating a workflow state transition on a content item"
input BeginTransitionInput {
    "ID of the collection to transition (mutually exclusive with metadataId)"
    collectionId: UUID
    "BCP 47 language tag for language-specific transitions"
    languageTag: String
    "ID of the metadata item to transition (mutually exclusive with collectionId)"
    metadataId: UUID
    "Whether to restart the transition if it has already been attempted"
    restart: Boolean
    "The target state ID to transition to"
    stateId: String!
    "Timestamp when this state becomes valid"
    stateValid: DateTime
    "Current status string for the transition"
    status: String!
    "Optional supplementary ID related to this transition"
    supplementaryId: String
    "Version of the metadata item to transition"
    version: Int
}

"Input for creating or importing a complete Bible translation, including all books, chapters, languages, and styles"
